## Headline

Total: 8 + 9 + 6 + 5 + 5 + 3 + 2 + 5 = 43 / 80  (54%)
Per-target 10/10 average: 5.4 / 10
Moonshot headline: 5.4 / 10 — past slogan, below operational.

## Threshold policy

If any line drops below 4/10 for two consecutive daily runs, raise
to a sprint-blocker. If the headline drops below 5/10, block the
next release per RULES.oot §1.17 (80/20 — most leverage is in the
lowest lines first).

## What closes each gap

1. No trust without proof → run 8D Red Team in CI; auto-fail drift.
2. Capabilities → 8-D env-var cap probe; CHANGES.md review.
3. Contracts → muse; outside this session.
4. Reproducible builds → **Move 1 of this session**: create the 4
   governance_*.oo, add per-repo ci.yml in openOODA, force
   v2.10.11 + vgovernance-v1.0.12 to ship, then pin the 10
   consumers.
5. Even evidence is verified → **Move 2 of this session**: wire
   `blackbox autopsy` as a post-step in every consumer ci.yml;
   make the double-run a CI gate.
6. Self-hosting → oodac_pure_build is the bridge; oodac must
   build oodac_pure_build then oodac then oodac_pure_build, hash
   equal. Owned by muse.
7. Multi-target → on ROADMAP.oot; owned by muse.
8. Per-target 10/10 → **Move 3 of this session**: this file +
   proof_of_today.oo driver; CI runs it daily; the score is the
   score.

## What this scorecard is NOT

Not a marketing surface. Not a vanity metric. The score is the
score, even when it is 2/10. Subtract what earns nothing
(RULES.oot §1.17).
